# Semgrep ignore file — the committed, human-reviewable scan-scope config CI honors
# (.github/workflows/pipeline-ci.yml runs semgrep with `--config auto --severity ERROR`).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: Semgrep's BUILT-IN default ignore list excludes `tests/`, so the
# entire backend test suite was silently unscanned — a real coverage hole, and one that
# also breaks the pipeline's scan-scope reconciliation (every changed .py must appear in
# semgrep's paths.scanned). Declaring the ignore list explicitly here replaces that
# default: dependency/build/vendor noise stays out, but OUR code — including tests/ —
# is scanned. Test code handles credentials and builds requests; it deserves the net.
#
# This file is NOT a finding-waiver channel. Per-finding waivers are `# nosemgrep: <rule-id>`
# comments at the flagged line, so each suppression is visible in the diff at its own site.

# Version control / tooling metadata
.git/
.github/actions/**/node_modules/
.pipeline/

# Python virtualenvs, caches and build output
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# JS/vendored dependencies
node_modules/
vendor/
*.min.js

# Xcode / Swift build output (Swift is reduced-assurance for these scanners anyway)
.build/
DerivedData/
*.xcworkspace/
*.xcodeproj/

# Terraform local state and provider plugins (never the .tf sources themselves)
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
